<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 1760) <span class="when">Oct 22, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li>Under the hood: kept in step with Asobi 1.0 (1760).</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1757) <span class="when">Oct 22, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Record the Session checks first</b>: a microphone macOS won&#8217;t share, or Siri and Dictation off, is said before the meeting, not after. A recording that hears nothing says so within seconds.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1752) <span class="when">Oct 22, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed</b>: joining after the host put the review on a shot&#8217;s source, stopping on a frame now shows the full-resolution source frame.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1747) <span class="when">Oct 22, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Source frames from the host</b>: when the host puts the review on a shot&#8217;s source, stopping on a frame shows that frame from the source at full resolution, marked SOURCE. Playing shows the QuickTime.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1742) <span class="when">Oct 22, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Internal reviews</b>: when the host marks a review internal, a flip to source on your Mac shows for the whole room, and theirs show for you. INTERNAL beside LIVE says so.</li>
<li><b>Fixed</b>: a clip shown on its source in a review was saved (and kept in the crash-recovery copy) with the source&#8217;s input space, so the QuickTime reopened decoded as the EXR.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1737) <span class="when">Oct 22, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Flip to source</b> in a review without a passphrase: Flip to Source Media (&#8997;&#8984;F) or Flip All shows a clip&#8217;s source on your screen only, with a SOURCE badge, where the source is reachable from your Mac. The room keeps the review copy.</li>
<li><b>Paste a review link</b> (&#8984;V) into an empty window to join, or drag one in from a browser or a message.</li>
<li><b>Show Original Frame</b> (&#8997;R) on a review copy now says it is the review copy the host shared, not that it is the original.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1734) <span class="when">Oct 21, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Finding media</b> no longer takes a file whose name merely starts with the same eight letters for the one asked for.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1728) <span class="when">Oct 20, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Recording a session</b> no longer turns the call and the clip audio down on your Mac while it records.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
